From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 16:30:00 -0700
Subject: cam: TEMP CDM-submit pinpoint + CAMNOC QoS confirmation breadcrumbs

The post-ICC wedge fires between "config_hw begin" and the first
0040 bl_write print. Three evidence lines in one run:
1. Stage prints through cam_ife_mgr_config_hw (bw-blob updates run
   BEFORE the CDM submit and call the cpas icc vote path),
   cam_cdm_submit_bls, and cam_hw_cdm_submit_bl (entry, pending-BL
   register read, wait_for_bl_fifo, get_io_buf) to pinpoint the
   dying access.
2. The get_io_buf print doubles as the SMMU discriminator: the
   lookup is against the CDM's own iommu handle, so rc=0 with a
   valid iova proves the BL buffer is mapped in the CDM's domain.
3. cam_cpastop_poweron readback of safe_lut/qosgen_mainctl for every
   enabled CAMNOC port plus the camnoc_info selection print settles
   whether TITAN_170_V200 QoS actually programs.
REMOVE when root-caused.
---

